Error [jet.AppPermissionPurpose]: `app.ask` may ask for the `camera` permission, but the package's `purposes:` doesn't say why.
  --> Tests/UI/app_permission_without_a_purpose.jet:3:43
    |
  3 | run: fn() -[Env, Net, Time]> { _: app.ask(.Camera) }
    |                                           ^^^^^^^
 Why: When the app asks for a device permission, the system shows the person why the app wants it, and a phone build writes the same text into its manifest; a permission the app asks for with no purpose has nothing to show. 
 Fix: Say why in the package's `purposes:` (for example `camera: "…"`), or remove the call.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-APP-PERMISSION-PURPOSE
